# CODEOWNERS
#
# The point of this file in an agentic repo is narrow and specific: an agent must not be able
# to widen its own guardrails without a human looking at it. Everything that defines what
# agents may do — their profiles, their instructions, the workflows that gate their output —
# is owned here.
#
# Two things to know:
#
#  1. Ownership alone does not block anything. It only requests a review. The block comes from
#     enabling "Require review from Code Owners" in the `main-protection` ruleset. That is off
#     by default in this repo, because a solo maintainer cannot approve their own pull request
#     and would deadlock. Turn it on before running the agent-authored-PR lab
#     (docs/labs/06-guardrails.md), where the agent is the author and you are the reviewer.
#
#  2. Later rules win. Keep the catch-all first.

# Everything, by default.
*                           @florezflow

# --- Agent control surface --------------------------------------------------------------
# Changing any of these changes what an agent is permitted to do.
/AGENTS.md                  @florezflow
/CLAUDE.md                  @florezflow
/.github/agents/            @florezflow
/.github/instructions/      @florezflow
/.github/copilot-instructions.md  @florezflow
/.claude/                   @florezflow
/.mcp.json                  @florezflow

# --- CI/CD control surface --------------------------------------------------------------
# Changing these changes the gates themselves, including whether they run at all.
/.github/workflows/         @florezflow
/.github/scripts/           @florezflow
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @florezflow
/ps-rule.yaml               @florezflow
/bicepconfig.json           @florezflow

# --- Production configuration -----------------------------------------------------------
/patterns/*/configurations/prod/   @florezflow
